WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.590
In most bowling alleys, one vendor’s system scores every frame and calls every foul.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:11.000
A bowler who thinks a call is wrong can only appeal to that same system.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.560
This paper asks whether a far cheaper rig, built independently, would agree.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.820
And when they disagree, whose call does the evidence favour?

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:26.210
We built ours from an infrared beam across the foul line at ankle height,

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.390
and a pressure mat under the approach.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.100
Its parts cost forty-six dollars a lane.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.090
It shadowed the alley’s system on six lanes for a thirty-two-week season:

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.760
thirty-eight thousand, five hundred and two frames.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.300
On clean frames, the two agreed almost perfectly.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.300
On the eight hundred and seventy-four disputed frames,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.660
agreement fell to fair.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.339
We took two hundred and eighty disputed frames,

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:54.259
and two reviewers watched each one in slow motion,

00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:56.549
blind to both systems’ calls.

00:00:57.349 --> 00:01:00.679
Against the video, the rig’s call matched fifty-three per cent of the time,

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:02.649
the alley’s own, fifty-five.

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:04.199
Both close to a coin flip.

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:08.209
The league’s rules committee ruled on all eight hundred and seventy-four.

00:01:08.709 --> 00:01:12.869
Ninety-one per cent of the time, it upheld the alley’s original call.

00:01:13.669 --> 00:01:17.279
The authors read the gap as a process tracking which system was already installed,

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:18.799
not which was more often right.

00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:22.639
A comparator only tells you two systems disagree.

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:25.309
It doesn’t tell a committee which one to believe,

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:27.899
and ours evidently didn’t change that.
